#show: worksheet.with(
  title: [Balancing Chemical Equations],
  subject: [Chemistry],
  grade: [Grade 9],
  instructions: [Balance each equation by writing coefficients in front of the formulas. Never change the subscripts. Write the balanced equation on the line.],
)

#callout(kind: "remember", title: [How to balance])[
  + Count the atoms of each element on both sides.
  + Change only the *coefficients* (the big numbers in front), never the small subscripts.
  + Balance elements that appear in only one substance first, and leave oxygen and hydrogen for last.
  + Check that every element has the same number of atoms on both sides.
]

= Level 1: Warm-up

